%global commit @COMMIT@
%global debug_package %{nil}
%global _build_id_links none

Name:           libssc
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        @RPMREL@%{?dist}
Summary:        Library and CLI for the sensors of the Qualcomm Snapdragon Sensor Core
License:        GPL-3.0-or-later
URL:            https://codeberg.org/DylanVanAssche/libssc
Source0:        libssc-%{commit}.tar.gz
# The project's fixes to the synchronous API (payload/sensors/libssc/; docs/sensors.md, Known issues): the wait
# blocks instead of spinning, each request owns its report handler, the subclasses reset theirs on open and close.
Patch0:         0001-common-block-in-the-synchronous-wait-instead-of-spinning.patch
Patch1:         0002-sensor-keep-each-request-s-report-handler-in-its-own-context.patch
Patch2:         0003-sensors-reset-the-report-handler-on-open-and-close.patch
ExclusiveArch:  aarch64

BuildRequires:  gcc
BuildRequires:  meson >= 1.4.0
BuildRequires:  ninja-build
BuildRequires:  pkgconf-pkg-config
BuildRequires:  pkgconfig(glib-2.0) >= 2.56
BuildRequires:  pkgconfig(gio-unix-2.0)
BuildRequires:  pkgconfig(qmi-glib) >= 1.33.4
BuildRequires:  pkgconfig(libprotobuf-c)
# protoc plus the protoc-gen-c plugin generate the message code
BuildRequires:  protobuf-compiler
BuildRequires:  protobuf-c-compiler
# The QMI mocking server for the test suite is declared unconditionally in meson (python module)
BuildRequires:  python3-devel

%description
libssc exposes the sensors managed by the Qualcomm Snapdragon Sensor Core, the
sensor framework running on the ADSP or SLPI of Qualcomm SoCs since 2018, as a
GLib library: QMI over QRTR to the DSP, protobuf-encoded requests. ssccli reads
one sensor from the command line (--sensor accelerometer|gyroscope|magnetometer|
light|compass|proximity). Upstream commit %{commit} plus the project's three
patches to the synchronous API. iio-sensor-proxy 3.9 builds its SSC drivers
against this library.

%package devel
Summary:        Development files for libssc
Requires:       %{name}%{?_isa} = %{version}-%{release}
Requires:       pkgconfig(qmi-glib)
Requires:       pkgconfig(gio-2.0)

%description devel
Headers and pkg-config file for building against libssc.

%prep
%autosetup -p1 -n libssc-%{commit}

%build
%meson
%meson_build

%install
%meson_install
# The QMI mocking server exists for the test suite, which needs a QRTR bus; not shipped.
rm -rf %{buildroot}%{python3_sitelib}/ssc_server %{buildroot}%{_libexecdir}/installed-tests \
       %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/installed-tests

%files
%license LICENSE
%doc README.md CHANGELOG.md
%{_libdir}/libssc.so.2*
%{_bindir}/ssccli

%files devel
%{_includedir}/libssc/
%{_libdir}/libssc.so
%{_libdir}/pkgconfig/libssc.pc

%changelog
* Wed Oct 07 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - @VERSION@-@RPMREL@
- Synchronous API: the wait blocks on the main context instead of spinning (iio-sensor-proxy at 92 %% of a core);
  each request keeps its own report handler, so two requests in flight on one sensor no longer disconnect each
  other's handler and leave a freed context connected (the proxy's hang in open_sync and its SIGSEGV in
  report_received); the sensor subclasses reset their handler on open and close and drop the client reference
  they leaked

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 0.4.4-2.git54dd13e.sp11
- Package upstream libssc for the Surface Pro 11 sensors stack (Fedora has no package)
